WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.085 --> 00:00:11.799
That evening Mateo made a special dinner to welcome his mother home.

2
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:18.260
"This is delicious," Ally said between mouthfuls. "What do you call this dish?"

3
00:00:18.261 --> 00:00:21.033
"Chicken piccata," Mateo said.

4
00:00:21.034 --> 00:00:23.873
"It's Dawn's favorite," Ray said.

5
00:00:23.874 --> 00:00:29.234
"It was," Dawn corrected him. "I discovered a new favorite in the city.

6
00:00:29.235 --> 00:00:35.297
There's a Japanese restaurant that serves delicious sushi. I can't wait for you to try it!"

7
00:00:35.298 --> 00:00:40.840
Ray smiled politely and so did Mateo, but neither one looked as excited as Dawn.

8
00:00:40.841 --> 00:00:46.442
"It sounds like Dawn likes the city much better than Sandville," Ally thought.

9
00:00:46.443 --> 00:00:49.127
"I wonder if she even wants to be here."

10
00:00:49.128 --> 00:00:54.815
Ally tried to read Dawn's mind, but she couldn't get a clear signal.

11
00:00:54.816 --> 00:00:59.530
It was just like yesterday, when she'd tried to read Ray's thoughts.

12
00:00:59.531 --> 00:01:05.190
Maybe humans' thoughts were hard to read if they had lots of different feelings at once.

13
00:01:05.191 --> 00:01:12.403
The meal continued in silence, until at last, everyone had finished eating.

14
00:01:12.404 --> 00:01:19.079
Ally and Mateo got up to clear the table, but Ray stopped them. "We'll clean up. You kids can go."

15
00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:24.743
Relieved, Ally and Mateo went to her room.

16
00:01:24.744 --> 00:01:28.300
"That was a good meal," Ally said. But

17
00:01:28.301 --> 00:01:35.547
Mateo looked glum. "The chicken piccata was good, but now my mom likes sushi better. And

18
00:01:35.548 --> 00:01:39.909
I overheard her talking about moving to the city. For good!" "Oh

19
00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:45.291
no," Ally said. "Then you'd live far from her permanently." "Nope,"

20
00:01:45.292 --> 00:01:51.446
Mateo said. "Because she wants Papi and me to move with her." "What?"

21
00:01:51.447 --> 00:01:55.822
Ally blinked. "But what about the diner?" "Papi

22
00:01:55.823 --> 00:02:04.126
doesn't want to sell it or move to the city. He loves Sandville." Mateo sighed. "He's

23
00:02:04.127 --> 00:02:08.304
so conflicted. I don't want to move either!" Ally

24
00:02:08.305 --> 00:02:14.204
jumped to her feet. "An Astralian's prime directive is to solve conflicts. I

25
00:02:14.205 --> 00:02:19.575
will be a good Astralian and convince Dawn that your family needs to stay here!" "That

26
00:02:19.576 --> 00:02:23.179
would be great!" Mateo looked relieved. "Thanks,

27
00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:28.323
Ally. Oh, and I almost forgot. I was on my space group chat earlier. People

28
00:02:28.324 --> 00:02:33.359
are saying that Lainie Polk might launch her P.O.D. from the Sandville desert." "Really?"

29
00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.783
Ally couldn't believe her luck. Mateo

30
00:02:36.784 --> 00:02:39.316
nodded. "And there's more. She

31
00:02:39.317 --> 00:02:44.437
might be planning to land on a planet called Carparia. Have you heard of it?" "Yes!

32
00:02:44.438 --> 00:02:49.554
Carparia is near Astralia! Or

33
00:02:49.555 --> 00:02:56.655
I think it is. I get it mixed up with Camparia." Ally switched Alpha on. "Alpha,

34
00:02:56.656 --> 00:03:02.797
which is closer to Astralia—Camparia or Carparia?" "Camping

35
00:03:02.798 --> 00:03:06.412
is popular with humans," Alpha said. "Ugh,

36
00:03:06.413 --> 00:03:16.228
not again!" Ally sighed. "Her glitches are getting worse." She turned off Alpha. "Either

37
00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:20.637
way, both planets are closer to Astralia than Earth is. If

38
00:03:20.638 --> 00:03:27.149
I can get to a nearby planet, I can use its technology to contact my parents. Then

39
00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:29.831
they can come and get me." "This

40
00:03:29.832 --> 00:03:32.878
could be your ticket home!" Mateo said. "We've

41
00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:41.585
got to find out if these rumors are true. I'll keep checking the chat for news." ***

42
00:03:41.586 --> 00:03:46.238
" Goood morning, Sandville!" a radio announcer

43
00:03:46.239 --> 00:03:51.033
said. "It's 79 degrees, and the sun is shining this fine

44
00:03:51.034 --> 00:03:55.492
morning!" "Turn that down, Alpha!" Ally covered her

45
00:03:55.493 --> 00:04:00.586
ears. "It's too early for the news. Play my morning dance music,

46
00:04:00.587 --> 00:04:04.644
please." But Alpha kept playing the

47
00:04:04.645 --> 00:04:08.959
news. "I wish I could get you to work like your old self," Ally

48
00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:13.296
said. She was about to turn Alpha off when the radio announcer said something

49
00:04:13.297 --> 00:04:16.561
else: Exciting things are happening in Sandville today!

50
00:04:16.562 --> 00:04:20.272
Several people have reported seeing large trucks parked in the desert.

51
00:04:20.273 --> 00:04:25.444
And a work crew is constructing something that can only be described as a spaceship.

52
00:04:25.445 --> 00:04:31.178
Is it possible that billionaire Lainie Polk will be launching her P.O.D. from the Sandville desert?

53
00:04:31.179 --> 00:04:35.060
Stay tuned to KSNV for more breaking news!

54
00:04:35.061 --> 00:04:40.397
Ally squealed with joy and raced toward Mateo's room.

55
00:04:40.398 --> 00:04:43.724
But Mateo was already on his way to her room.

56
00:04:43.725 --> 00:04:47.648
"Did you hear the news?" they both cried at once.

57
00:04:47.649 --> 00:04:51.397
"What's all the excitement about?" Ray called from the kitchen.

58
00:04:51.398 --> 00:04:55.949
"Nothing, Papi!" Mateo said as he and Ally ducked into her room.

59
00:04:55.950 --> 00:05:01.254
"We have to find a way to get you on that P.O.D.," Mateo said.

60
00:05:01.255 --> 00:05:03.787
"But how?" Ally asked.

61
00:05:03.788 --> 00:05:09.823
"I don't know, but we're not going to stop working on a plan until we get you a ride back to space!"

62
00:05:09.824 --> 00:05:13.162
Mateo vowed. "And we can start right now by—"

63
00:05:13.163 --> 00:05:16.224
"Hey, Ally!" Ray knocked lightly on the door.

64
00:05:16.225 --> 00:05:19.728
"I'll drive you to work today. We'll leave in 15 minutes."

65
00:05:19.729 --> 00:05:30.396
Ally groaned. "Oh well. I guess we'll start working on that plan later!"

